IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting Act (Amendment of First Schedule) Notification 2012 (S 549/2012), made under section 65 of the Broadcasting Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-amendment-of-first-schedule-notification-2012/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S549-2012.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited).
-- It was made on 30 October 2012, first published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 31 October 2012 at 5.00 pm, and (paragraph 1) "shall be deemed to have come into operation on 1st January 2011".
-- The within-day detail (5.00 pm) is not kept: the reading day is a date. Whether a retrospective notification is valid, and what a court would do with conduct already past, is not addressed here.

§ `Paragraphs 1 and 2: the First Schedule deleted and a new one substituted`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 31st October 2012 at 5.00 pm.
-- src:19 | Citation and commencement
-- src:20 | 1. This Notification may be cited as the Broadcasting Act
-- src:21 | (Amendment of First Schedule) Notification 2012 and shall be deemed
-- src:22 | to have come into operation on 1st January 2011.
-- src:24 | Deletion and substitution of First Schedule
-- src:25 | 2. The First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act is deleted and
-- src:26 | the following Schedule substituted therefor:
-- src:27 | ‘‘FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:28 | Section 2(1)
-- src:29 | BROADCASTING APPARATUS
-- src:31 | 1. Television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system).
-- src:32 | In this Schedule, ‘‘television receive-only satellite receiving system’’ means
-- src:33 | any apparatus (including a dish antenna) or any combination of apparatus
-- src:34 | capable of direct reception of any broadcasting service emitted from or passing
-- src:35 | through any communication or broadcast satellite in extra-terrestrial space.’’.
-- src:37 | Made this 30th day of October 2012.
@ref S 549/2012 publication line, paras 1 and 2 and the date made (src:3-37)
`the First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012` MEANS
    `First Schedule version` WITH `source` IS "S 549/2012, made 30 October 2012, first published 31 October 2012 at 5.00 pm, deemed in operation from 1 January 2011"
                                 , `takes effect on` IS (Date 1 1 2011)
                                 , `published on` IS (Date 31 10 2012)
                                 , `lists broadcast television receivers` IS FALSE
                                 , `lists broadcast sound receivers` IS FALSE
                                 , `lists TVRO systems` IS TRUE
